  "version": "0.5.3-beta.11",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.3-beta.10`\n\n### Features\n\n- let Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and pi tell tTerm when they work, wait for the user, finish or fail, through hooks and plugins installed from the notification settings that write the report to their own terminal, so tabs show the agent's state and its waits and finished turns are announced, also inside tmux ([3f9426e9](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/3f9426e9144c6e61708ef5dbdf801bb391b62430))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- let terminal, SFTP and editor shortcuts act on the focused split pane only instead of on every pane in sight, which cleared, reset, searched or filled a saved password into all of them, and put the keyboard in a pane in sight once it becomes the focused one from the tab bar, a shortcut or a closed tab ([e19acfb4](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e19acfb476f4a154bc4a82ecf2f70461af14e96c))\n- announce notifications from a split pane in sight while the user types in another one, closing the toast once that pane gets the focus, and put the keyboard in the terminal a notification leads back to instead of leaving it on the closed toast or the other pane ([67992341](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/6799234132e256634de168d617429feeb5de5865))\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- show toasts in the top right under the tab bar and the split pane headers instead of over the tabs, keep them open while the pointer is on them or the window is in the background, close a tab's toast once the user looks at the tab, and stack up to a configurable number of them, three by default ([aee8cbe0](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/aee8cbe0234e3636d93b4e22d0b16bd76b0ecbd8))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.3-beta.10...v0.5.3-beta.11](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.3-beta.10...v0.5.3-beta.11)",
